WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.900
 Hello, Marvel fans.

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.100
We're here with
Benedict Cumberbatch

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.240
who plays Doctor Strange.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.590
You have had quite the
busy life, my friend.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:06.390
 Yep.

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:09.360
 What is it like to dive
into the Marvel multiverse?

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.050
 Marvel is a fun place to be
right now as Doctor Strange.

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:14.070
That's all I will say.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:17.520
And yeah, you know,
he brings something

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.860
very interesting to this film.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.350
But most of all, having worked
with Tom, not just on this,

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.270
but on a couple
of other projects,

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.990
it's just wonderful to
be by his side again

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:26.790
and doing what we do.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.790
And establishing and maturing
and growing that relationship

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:30.690
is fantastic.

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.220
 What is it like
bringing Doctor Strange

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.680
into the world of Spider-Man?

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:35.500
 A lot of fun.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.300
A lot of fun.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.890
You know, I get to play the
grown up surrounded by kids.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:39.690
I can say that.

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.370
They're half my
age, they are kids.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:42.990
I'm blown away by
their professionalism,

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.400
by the atmosphere
they create on set,

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.290
by the fun it is
to be on that set.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.720
Jon Watts is a
phenomenal director.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.130
He's such a joy to work with.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:51.960
He really, he's great
on the granular,

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.430
he gives you context
to understand

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.710
where your place is in the
story and the development of it.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:57.300
Even when all the story
hasn't been finished,

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.000
which is often the way with
these films at the time

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.150
of production starting.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:02.910
And it is just fun
from start to finish.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.010
 What goes through
Doctor Strange's mind

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.200
after saving worlds
and universes,

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.220
a young Peter Parker
comes up saying, hey,

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:11.610
can you craft a spell
to have people forget?

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.110
 I think the most that
goes through his mind

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.623
is to see in the
film, it's like yeah,

00:01:14.623 --> 00:01:15.690
sure I want to help you out kid.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:16.710
You did great back there.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:19.630
And you're one of them and
us and you know, we're doing,

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:20.800
we're all on the same team here.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.890
So sure I'll help a friend out.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.990
It doesn't really take
into account that he's

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.880
still a kid at high school.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.350
And in trying to people please,
or going yeah, OK, let's

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.330
do one for the team, yeah.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:36.630
Some crazy stuff is unleashed.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.280
And that's where
the relationship

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.763
starts to evolve and mature.

00:01:39.763 --> 00:01:41.130
And that's what I'm
really excited about.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:43.170
I mean, there's
some crazy reveals

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:46.140
and fun spills and
thrills in this, but also,

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.580
for me as an actor,
the thing that

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.680
matters most is that emotional
connection to a character

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:53.020
and the people who
surround him and the world

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:53.820
that surrounds him.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.120
So with Tom and I, that's a
really beautiful relationship

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.090
that's kicking off.

